  "body": "CONTEMPORARY FAMILY PERFECTION\r\n\r\nThe vendor is highly motivated to sell and welcomes all offers; conjunctional agents are invited to collaborate - their loss will be your gain.\r\n\r\nThose with an eye for refined contemporary design and a love of quality finishes will be drawn to this rare opportunity: a sun-soaked, circa-2000's, two-storey executive home on a 438sqm freehold section, perfectly positioned between The Bays, the CBD and the airport.\r\n\r\nSet at the end of a private ROW and framed by lush, manicured tropical gardens, this 213sqm stately residence makes a striking first impression. A grand portico and heavy high-stud double entrance doors open to an expansive foyer, immediately showcasing the home’s generous proportions and sophisticated style.\r\n\r\nDesigned for effortless year-round entertaining, the open-plan designer kitchen, chic dining area and elegant living room are anchored by a dramatic mantled fireplace and spill seamlessly to the sun-drenched outdoor spaces. The result is outstanding indoor/outdoor flow and an easy, resort-like lifestyle.\r\n\r\nDownstairs also features a generous interlinking entrance hall, soaring ceilings and a guest powder room, or separate living  area. while a sweeping staircase leads to the private accommodation wing above. Upstairs here you’ll find three oversized double bedrooms and a well-appointed family bathroom.\r\n\r\nThe luxurious master suite is a true retreat, with walk-in wardrobe, double-vanity ensuite and direct access to a cabana-style sun deck overlooking the tropical garden - the perfect spot for morning coffee or evening relaxation.\r\n\r\nThoughtfully constructed with a cavity wall-system roughcast exterior, the home is completed by carpeted internal-access garaging for two cars, plus a sauna with shower - ideal after a day at the beach. There is ample off-street parking for additional vehicles and a boat.\r\n\r\nOrakei’s central location offers coveted access to top public and private schooling, and a superb coastal lifestyle. Stroll to the waterfront and enjoy nearby Mission Bay, Kohimarama and St Heliers with their beautiful beaches, parks, cafes and restaurants. Everyday convenience is covered by Eastridge Shopping Centre, with its supermarket and excellent mix of local shops and eateries.\r\n\r\nIf a prime address in a tropical garden setting, easy beach walks and an executive-level home are high on your wish list, this property deserves to be at the very top. Make sure you are at the auction.\r\n\r\nFor further information on this outstanding home or local insights to assist with your decision in this sought-after seaside suburb, please call me!",
